[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605281900-kotoba-subrepo-charter-rider-reconciliation", :adr/title "ADR-2605281900: kotoba subrepo Charter Rider reconciliation — upstream Rider removal vs ADR-2605192200 invariant", :adr/status "proposed-pending-council-ratification", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605281900: kotoba subrepo Charter Rider reconciliation\n\n**Status**: proposed-pending-council-ratification\n**Date**: 2026-05-28\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (Founder Lv7+; emergency authorization **NOT taken**)\n\n# Context\n\n## 1.1 Upstream change\n\n`git subrepo pull 40-engine/kotoba` (commit `5e05ac98f`, 2026-05-28) brought upstream `etzhayyim/kotoba@a673a8ce6` which **removed all per-crate `NOTICE` and `CHARTER-RIDER.md` files** from the kotoba workspace:\n\n- 17 crate-level `CHARTER-RIDER.md` symlinks deleted\n- 17 crate-level `NOTICE` files deleted\n- Repo-root `CHARTER-RIDER.md` symlink deleted\n- Repo-root `NOTICE` deleted\n\nThe kotoba subrepo's workspace and per-crate `Cargo.toml` still declare `license = \"Apache-2.0\"` (workspace-inherited via `license.workspace = true`), but the **co-distributed NOTICE files acknowledging the etzhayyim Charter Compliance Rider v2.0 are absent**.\n\n## 1.2 ADR-2605192200 §3.4 invariant\n\nADR-2605192200 v2.0 §3.4 requires:\n\n> Every Apache-2.0-licensed first-party package in `etzhayyim/root` MUST carry a NOTICE referencing CHARTER-RIDER.md (symlink to repo-root permitted). The retro-active applicator at `70-tools/charter-rider-applicator/apply.sh` enforces this on the entire monorepo.\n\nThe monorepo root `/CHARTER-RIDER.md` itself is preserved (intact at `Users/junkawasaki/github/etzhayyim-root/CHARTER-RIDER.md`). The deletion is **scoped to the kotoba subrepo path** `40-engine/kotoba/**`.\n\n## 1.3 Session decision sequence\n\nWithin the same session:\n\n1. `5e05ac98f` (subrepo pull) — landed the upstream deletion\n2. `3beff8bdf` (charter-rider re-application) — restored NOTICE + Rider symlinks across all 21 kotoba dirs via scoped `apply.sh`-equivalent run\n3. **User instruction 2026-05-28**: \"kotoba subrepo は remote を優先\" (the kotoba subrepo should defer to upstream)\n4. `a4bb5cf89` (revert of `3beff8bdf`) — removed the re-applied Rider files, returning the subrepo to upstream-pristine state\n\nCurrent state at HEAD = subrepo content matches upstream `etzhayyim/kotoba@a673a8ce6` byte-for-byte; **the constitutional gap remains open**.\n\n# Decision\n\nThis ADR **does not** amend ADR-2605192200 §3.4 unilaterally. It:\n\n1. **Records** the deviation as an explicit, time-bounded exception\n2. **Scopes** the resolution path\n3. **Proposes** an §3.4 amendment for **Council Lv6+ ≥3 ratification** (Founder Lv7+ emergency authorization explicitly NOT taken — institutional integrity over expediency, mirroring ADR-2605262200 precedent)\n\n## 5.1 Deviation acknowledgment\n\nUntil Council ratifies one of §5.2's paths, the following holds:\n\n- **D1**: The kotoba subrepo at `40-engine/kotoba/**` is **in known non-compliance** with ADR-2605192200 §3.4 NOTICE+Rider attachment invariant.\n- **D2**: The monorepo root `/CHARTER-RIDER.md` and `/NOTICE` are preserved, intact, and authoritative for the religious-corp's Apache-2.0 + Rider distribution as a whole.\n- **D3**: All non-subrepo'd Apache-2.0 packages in `etzhayyim/root` (everything outside `40-engine/kotoba/**`) **remain compliant** per the existing `70-tools/charter-rider-applicator/` enforcement.\n- **D4**: The Rider's substantive 8-prohibited-category constraint set (§2(a)-(h)) **continues to apply to kotoba code authorship**; the gap is purely about NOTICE attachment, not about substantive compliance. Anyone using or extending kotoba within etzhayyim/root remains bound by §2(a)-(h) via the monorepo-root Rider.\n\n## 5.2 Proposed resolution paths (Council to choose)\n\n### Path A — §3.4 amendment: subrepo'd packages may rely on root-only Rider\n\nAmend ADR-2605192200 §3.4 to add a carve-out:\n\n> Packages pulled in via git-subrepo from a religious-corp-controlled upstream (e.g., `github.com/etzhayyim/kotoba`) MAY satisfy §3.4 by relying solely on the monorepo-root NOTICE + CHARTER-RIDER.md, provided that:\n> - the upstream is itself religious-corp-controlled (not a third-party fork)\n> - the upstream's own LICENSE remains Apache-2.0\n> - the upstream's README or top-level documentation references the etzhayyim Charter Compliance Rider (advisory, not strict)\n> - 70-tools/charter-rider-applicator/verify.sh is updated to skip git-subrepo paths\n>\n> Threshold: Council Lv6+ ≥3 attestation per ADR-2605192200 v2.0 §6 amendment policy.\n\n**Pros**: minimal local divergence; future `git subrepo pull` operations succeed without conflict; clean push-back path.\n\n**Cons**: weakens the per-crate NOTICE invariant. Downstream consumers cloning only the kotoba subrepo (not the monorepo) would not see the Rider unless the upstream's own README references it.\n\n### Path B — upstream PR: re-add NOTICE+Rider in `etzhayyim/kotoba` itself\n\nOpen a PR against `github.com/etzhayyim/kotoba@main` that restores `NOTICE` + `CHARTER-RIDER.md` at the kotoba repo root + each crate dir. Since the upstream is religious-corp-controlled, this is a procedural step, not a third-party dependency negotiation.\n\n**Pros**: full §3.4 compliance restored, no amendment required.\n\n**Cons**: re-creates the local-vs-upstream conflict pattern that the user's \"remote 優先\" instruction asked us to avoid. Adds a maintenance burden on every `subrepo pull` if the upstream maintainer regresses.\n\n### Path C — kotoba subrepo Rider overlay (local-only, not pushed upstream)\n\nRe-apply Rider locally as in revert commit `3beff8bdf` did, but mark the additions as **explicitly not part of `git subrepo push` candidates** (e.g., via a `.gitrepo` `ignore-pattern` or a wrapper script that filters them out before push).\n\n**Pros**: per-crate compliance restored locally; upstream cleanliness preserved.\n\n**Cons**: git-subrepo lacks first-class \"ignore certain paths from push\" support; would require maintaining a custom wrapper. High operational fragility.\n\n### Path D — defer permanently with explicit constitutional carve-out\n\nAccept the deletion as the new baseline. Amend ADR-2605192200 to drop the per-package NOTICE invariant entirely for first-party religious-corp packages.\n\n**Pros**: simplest. Aligns with \"remote 優先\" precedent.\n\n**Cons**: substantive weakening of the Rider's constitutional weight. Almost certainly fails Council Lv6+ ratification given Charter §1.5 (open-source pluralism + multi-generational reproducibility).\n\n## 5.3 Recommended path\n\n**Path A** (§3.4 carve-out amendment) — preserves the substantive Rider constraints (§2(a)-(h)) while accommodating the upstream-religious-corp-controlled-subrepo pattern that ADR-2605262130 made canonical. Path B is a fallback if Council prefers strict §3.4. Paths C and D are not recommended.\n\n# Consequences\n\n## 6.1 Until Council ratification\n\n- The `verify.sh` script (currently flagging kotoba subrepo paths as Rider-missing) is **expected to surface this gap**. Operators reading verify output should reference this ADR, not interpret the gap as an unknown drift.\n- New `subrepo pull` operations on kotoba **MUST NOT** re-apply Rider per `apply.sh` unilaterally (the revert `a4bb5cf89` set the local baseline).\n- All other monorepo paths remain under the unchanged §3.4 invariant — `apply.sh` continues to enforce, `verify.sh` continues to validate.\n\n## 6.2 If Path A ratified\n\n- Update `70-tools/charter-rider-applicator/apply.sh` to skip `40-engine/kotoba/**` (and any future git-subrepo'd path detectable via `.gitrepo` marker file).\n- Update `verify.sh` symmetrically.\n- Update `CHARTER-RIDER.md` itself with a new §appendix documenting the carve-out criteria.\n- Update CLAUDE.md \"Do Not\" section to qualify the Rider invariant accordingly.\n\n## 6.3 Risk\n\n| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Downstream consumer clones only kotoba subrepo, misses Rider | Medium | Path A's \"upstream README references Rider\" advisory clause; upstream kotoba README already cites `etzhayyim/root` repo |\n| Council declines all paths | Medium | Default to Path B (upstream PR); accept the operational cost |\n| Future subrepo pulls regress | Low | Verify.sh + lefthook hook + this ADR's documentation form the standing review surface |\n| ADR-2605192200 v2.0 itself becomes Lv7+ unanimity locked further | Low | §3.4 amendment is §6 Lv6+; §2(a)-(h) substantive list remains Lv7+ |\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\nPath C (local overlay) and Path D (drop the invariant) are documented in §5.2 and explicitly not recommended.\n\nA fifth alternative — abandon kotoba in favor of a parallel substrate that retains per-crate Rider — was not seriously considered: kotoba is the canonical storage substrate per ADR-2605262130 with 17+ crates of religious-corp-authored work, and substitution cost exceeds the §3.4 amendment cost by orders of magnitude.\n\n# References\n\n- ADR-2605192200 (Charter Compliance Rider v2.0 — the invariant being reconciled)\n- ADR-2605262130 (kotoba storage substrate unification — makes kotoba canonical)\n- ADR-2605192300 (Bootstrap Council — Lv6+ threshold)\n- ADR-2605192100 (Mission Charter — Charter §1.5 open-source pluralism context)\n- ADR-2605262200 (procedural precedent for \"Founder Lv7+ emergency authorization explicitly NOT taken\")\n- Commit `5e05ac98f` (subrepo pull that brought the deletion)\n- Commit `3beff8bdf` (re-application, then reverted)\n- Commit `a4bb5cf89` (revert, current baseline)\n- `40-engine/kotoba/.gitrepo` (subrepo metadata; `remote = https://github.com/etzhayyim/kotoba.git`)\n- `70-tools/charter-rider-applicator/{apply,verify}.sh` (target update points if Path A ratified)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605281900-kotoba-subrepo-charter-rider-reconciliation.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "charter-rider", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-28", :adr/date "2026-05-28", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605192100-etzhayyim-mission-charter"], :adr/authoritative_for ["reconciliation of upstream kotoba Rider deletion vs ADR-2605192200 invariant" "acceptable state of NOTICE+Rider attachment in git-subrepo'd Apache-2.0 packages"]}]
